1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:03,471
It's dues season at the Riverside Climbing Club.

2
00:00:03,471 --> 00:00:06,912
The money arrives on PayPal, and it arrives like this.

3
00:00:07,242 --> 00:00:09,500
Sixty dollars, for Max and Tom.

4
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:11,568
Thirty, from someone called Fabi.

5
00:00:11,748 --> 00:00:13,372
Lena, who paid twice.

6
00:00:13,552 --> 00:00:16,529
And fifteen from a stranger, for a bouldering trip.

7
00:00:17,009 --> 00:00:19,537
Someone has to work out who actually paid.

8
00:00:19,537 --> 00:00:23,390
In most clubs, that someone is a volunteer with a spreadsheet.

9
00:00:24,024 --> 00:00:27,434
Clubkeep is an AI treasurer that does that job for them.

10
00:00:27,814 --> 00:00:28,697
Here's the club.

11
00:00:28,697 --> 00:00:31,955
Fourteen members, four hundred and five dollars to collect,

12
00:00:31,955 --> 00:00:33,345
and nothing booked yet.

13
00:00:33,726 --> 00:00:34,619
One click.

14
00:00:34,999 --> 00:00:40,052
Clubkeep pulls every incoming payment through PayPal's Transaction Search API.

15
00:00:40,282 --> 00:00:43,735
Then a small language model, running on the club's own server,

16
00:00:43,735 --> 00:00:46,251
reads each note and matches it to a member.

17
00:00:46,481 --> 00:00:49,131
No member data goes to an AI company.

18
00:00:49,762 --> 00:00:52,349
Six of the ten payments are booked straight away,

19
00:00:52,349 --> 00:00:54,265
and every one shows its reasoning.

20
00:00:54,495 --> 00:00:56,487
Fabi is Fabian Ward's nickname.

21
00:00:56,867 --> 00:00:59,234
Leoni, with a typo, is Leonie Fischer.

22
00:00:59,965 --> 00:01:01,968
When it isn't sure, it doesn't guess.

23
00:01:01,968 --> 00:01:02,522
It asks.

24
00:01:02,802 --> 00:01:07,457
Sarah's sixty dollars is exactly two memberships, and the note names her kids.

25
00:01:07,637 --> 00:01:10,124
Confirm, and Max and Tom are both paid.

26
00:01:10,755 --> 00:01:13,068
Lena's second payment is a duplicate.

27
00:01:13,248 --> 00:01:17,856
Approve it, and Clubkeep sends her money back through the PayPal Payments API.

28
00:01:18,086 --> 00:01:20,699
The refund receipt stays attached to the decision.

29
00:01:21,029 --> 00:01:22,208
Mark isn't a member.

30
00:01:22,208 --> 00:01:25,749
His fifteen dollars was for a trip, so that goes back too.

31
00:01:26,379 --> 00:01:28,604
That leaves six people who still owe.

32
00:01:28,604 --> 00:01:30,409
Instead of an awkward message,

33
00:01:30,409 --> 00:01:33,477
each one gets a PayPal invoice with a pay button.

34
00:01:33,707 --> 00:01:36,812
Sophie was five dollars short, so hers is for five.

35
00:01:37,042 --> 00:01:39,955
Edit the note if you like, and send them all at once.

36
00:01:40,585 --> 00:01:42,247
When Sophie pays her invoice,

37
00:01:42,247 --> 00:01:45,519
Clubkeep picks it up from PayPal and marks her as paid.

38
00:01:46,399 --> 00:01:50,695
Every decision, and every PayPal call, is logged for the next treasurer.

39
00:01:51,331 --> 00:01:55,102
Clubkeep reads payments, refunds mistakes and sends invoices,

40
00:01:55,102 --> 00:01:56,397
all through PayPal.

41
00:01:56,627 --> 00:02:00,606
The AI explains itself, and nothing moves money without your click.

42
00:02:00,836 --> 00:02:02,784
It's open source, and free to run.

43
00:02:02,784 --> 00:02:05,884
An evening of spreadsheet work, done in two minutes.
